PyTorch (ROCm/pytorch release/2.8, commit d618db8): route torch._int_mm to
rocBLAS on gfx803 instead of hipBLASLt.

WHY
torch._int_mm (int8 x int8 -> int32) fails on every call on gfx803. On ROCm,
at::cuda::blas::int8_gemm calls hipBLASLt and has no other path, and
hipBLASLt has never shipped kernels for gfx803, so its heuristic query
returns HIPBLAS_STATUS_INVALID_VALUE:

  RuntimeError: CUDA error: HIPBLAS_STATUS_INVALID_VALUE when calling
  `hipblasLtMatmulAlgoGetHeuristic( ltHandle, ...`

TORCH_BLAS_PREFER_HIPBLASLT=0, which the base image sets, does not help:
int8_gemm never asks for the preferred backend, while the fp gemm, bgemm and
addmm paths in the same file do and fall back to rocBLAS. Anything that
quantizes a linear layer to int8 reaches it (ComfyUI's int8 backends, for
example). To reproduce, run torch._int_mm on two 1024x1024 int8 GPU tensors.

The fix and its analysis come from the upstream rocm-gfx803 project's ROCm 10
line (Schaka/rocm-gfx803 commit 5061404, written against torch 2.14). This is
the same change adapted to torch 2.8: 2.8 has neither
getHipblasltSupportedArchs() nor CUBLAS_SM_CARVEOUT_GUARD, so the rocBLAS path
is chosen with the check 2.8's own fp gemm paths use instead.

WHAT
int8_gemm calls rocblas_gemm_ex (i8 inputs, i32 output and compute) whenever
the preferred BLAS backend is not hipBLASLt. Context makes hipBLASLt the
preferred backend only on archs it supports (gfx90a, gfx942 and a few newer
ones) and falls back to rocBLAS elsewhere, so gfx803 always takes the rocBLAS
path, and archs that use hipBLASLt keep the Lt path unchanged. The call uses
the same handle, stream and column-major contract as the file's existing
rocblas_gemm_ex calls. rocBLAS 6.4.4 as built for gfx803 here carries int8
(I8I_HPA) Tensile kernels for all four transpose layouts.

REAL-HARDWARE VERIFICATION (RX 590, this image)
torch._int_mm on the GPU against an exact int64 CPU product: 18 of 18 cases
bit-exact (shapes from 17x8x8 to 2048x6144x2048, plain, transposed-A,
transposed-B and both, including odd sizes). Before the patch every one of
them raised the error above. 2048x2048x2048 runs in 4.24 ms (4.05 TOPS).

diff --git a/aten/src/ATen/cuda/CUDABlas.cpp b/aten/src/ATen/cuda/CUDABlas.cpp
index 573389b..7ef9ae9 100644
--- a/aten/src/ATen/cuda/CUDABlas.cpp
+++ b/aten/src/ATen/cuda/CUDABlas.cpp
@@ -1996,6 +1996,60 @@ void scaled_gemm(
   TORCH_CHECK(false, "scaled_gemm is only supported for CUDA 11.8 and above");
 }
 
+#ifdef USE_ROCM
+// GFX803_INT8_GEMM_ROCBLAS_PATCH: hipBLASLt ships no kernels for gfx803 (or
+// any arch it does not list), so the Lt heuristic query below fails there with
+// HIPBLAS_STATUS_INVALID_VALUE. rocBLAS carries int8 -> int32 Tensile kernels
+// for those archs, with the same column-major contract as the Lt call.
+static void int8_gemm_rocblas(
+    bool transpose_mat1,
+    bool transpose_mat2,
+    int64_t m,
+    int64_t n,
+    int64_t k,
+    const int8_t* mat1_ptr,
+    int64_t mat1_ld,
+    const int8_t* mat2_ptr,
+    int64_t mat2_ld,
+    int32_t* result_ptr,
+    int64_t result_ld) {
+  CUDABLAS_NONNEGINT_CHECK(int8_gemm, m);
+  CUDABLAS_NONNEGINT_CHECK(int8_gemm, n);
+  CUDABLAS_NONNEGINT_CHECK(int8_gemm, k);
+  CUDABLAS_POSINT_CHECK(int8_gemm, mat1_ld);
+  CUDABLAS_POSINT_CHECK(int8_gemm, mat2_ld);
+  CUDABLAS_POSINT_CHECK(int8_gemm, result_ld);
+  cublasHandle_t handle = at::cuda::getCurrentCUDABlasHandle();
+  int32_t alpha = 1;
+  int32_t beta = 0;
+  TORCH_CUDABLAS_CHECK(rocBLASStatusToHIPStatus(rocblas_gemm_ex(
+      (rocblas_handle)handle,
+      transpose_mat1 ? rocblas_operation_transpose : rocblas_operation_none,
+      transpose_mat2 ? rocblas_operation_transpose : rocblas_operation_none,
+      m,
+      n,
+      k,
+      &alpha,
+      mat1_ptr,
+      rocblas_datatype_i8_r,
+      mat1_ld,
+      mat2_ptr,
+      rocblas_datatype_i8_r,
+      mat2_ld,
+      &beta,
+      result_ptr,
+      rocblas_datatype_i32_r,
+      result_ld,
+      result_ptr,
+      rocblas_datatype_i32_r,
+      result_ld,
+      rocblas_datatype_i32_r,
+      rocblas_gemm_algo_standard,
+      0,
+      0)));
+}
+#endif
+
 void int8_gemm(
     bool transpose_mat1,
     bool transpose_mat2,
@@ -2008,6 +2062,17 @@ void int8_gemm(
     int64_t mat2_ld,
     int32_t* result_ptr,
     int64_t result_ld) {
+#ifdef USE_ROCM
+  // The same rule the fp gemm paths in this file follow: rocBLAS unless
+  // hipBLASLt is the preferred backend, which Context only allows on archs
+  // hipBLASLt supports.
+  if (at::globalContext().blasPreferredBackend() != BlasBackend::Cublaslt) {
+    int8_gemm_rocblas(
+        transpose_mat1, transpose_mat2, m, n, k,
+        mat1_ptr, mat1_ld, mat2_ptr, mat2_ld, result_ptr, result_ld);
+    return;
+  }
+#endif
 
   cublasComputeType_t computeType = CUBLAS_COMPUTE_32I;
   cudaDataType_t scaleType = CUDA_R_32I;
